	No, PLATO is not an Internet site.  It is a fairly old computer system
based in Champaign-Urbana, at the University of Illinois.  PLATO stands for
"Personalized Learning And Teaching <something>".  Its main use is providing
lessons on every concievable subject, from accounting to math to sign
language, and there are a number of popular games for after-hours use, 
including Avatar, the most awesome D&D-type game ever.


